191
00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:34.273
So the purpose of structured output
is to turn language model responses

192
00:09:34.273 --> 00:09:35.741
into programable data.

193
00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:40.741
So here's an example of a way that we can
program with our language model output.

194
00:09:41.047 --> 00:09:45.184
Here, we're going to construct a list to
contain all of the rows that we generate.

195
00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:48.988
We're going to iterate across dimensions
that our users have provided.

196
00:09:48.988 --> 00:09:52.224
We're going to analyze those mentioned
by creating these mentioned objects.

197
00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:55.695
If there's a response that is needed,
we can print out that we're responding

198
00:09:55.728 --> 00:09:58.364
to that user message
using the standard attributes

199
00:09:58.364 --> 00:10:01.867
from any Python class,
such as processed mention dot sentiment.

200
00:10:02.034 --> 00:10:05.004
If there's a support ticket,
we can print that out as well.

201
00:10:05.004 --> 00:10:08.007
Let's take a look
at how we program with our mentions. Here,

202
00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.043
we're going to iterate through each
of the mentions that we have available.

203
00:10:11.177 --> 00:10:14.046
We're going to call the LLM
to get a mention object

204
00:10:14.046 --> 00:10:16.015
that we can program with, right here.

205
00:10:16.015 --> 00:10:19.352
Then we're going to print out some
information about that process mentioned

206
00:10:19.352 --> 00:10:20.453
that's in the helper file.

207
00:10:20.453 --> 00:10:24.457
If you want to take a look. We're going to
convert our process data to a dictionary

208
00:10:24.457 --> 00:10:28.227
using pydantic tools in this case
the model dump method.

209
00:10:28.361 --> 00:10:32.031
Next, we're going to store this
original message in a data frame row.

210
00:10:32.064 --> 00:10:35.968
So we'll basically just be adding it
to this processed dict object.

211
00:10:36.102 --> 00:10:39.138
Then we're going to add that dictionary
to our list of rows.

212
00:10:39.472 --> 00:10:42.975
And then print out a blank row
so that we can read everything

213
00:10:42.975 --> 00:10:43.976
that gets printed out.

214
00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:46.846
So let's run
this and see what the result looks like.

215
00:10:46.846 --> 00:10:51.217
As we go through, we can see the model
responding to positive.=

216
00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.619
app feedback.
The negative website feedback.

217
00:10:53.619 --> 00:10:55.521
It will describe its responses

218
00:10:55.521 --> 00:10:59.258
and add support tickets if relevant
such as right here.

219
00:10:59.291 --> 00:11:01.560
The user has reported our website is down.

220
00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:04.530
And then of course
the user who has specified hey, at Tech

